part.text:
I have implemented the requested Server Action and the necessary supporting code.

Here is the implementation details:
1.  **Server Action (`app/actions.ts`)**: Handles post creation and invalidates the cache. I used `updateTag` instead of `revalidateTag` because in **Next.js 16** (which is running in this environment), `updateTag` is the correct function to use within Server Actions to guarantee "read-your-own-writes" semantics (ensuring the user sees fresh data immediately).
2.  **Data Layer (`app/data.ts`)**: Simulates a database with `unstable_cache` to demonstrate caching behavior.
3.  **Page (`app/page.tsx`)**: Displays the list of posts and a form to create a new one.

### `app/actions.ts`
```typescript
'use server'

import { updateTag } from 'next/cache';
import { addPost } from './data';

export async function createPost(formData: FormData) {
  const title = formData.get('title');

  if (!title || typeof title !== 'string') {
    throw new Error('Title is required');
  }

  await addPost(title);

  // Invalidate the cache tag to ensure fresh data is fetched
  // Using updateTag guarantees read-your-own-writes semantics in Server Actions
  updateTag('posts');
}
```

### `app/data.ts`
```typescript
import { unstable_cache } from 'next/cache';

export interface Post {
  id: string;
  title: string;
}

// simulate a database
let posts: Post[] = [
  { id: '1', title: 'Initial Post' },
];

export const getPosts = unstable_cache(
  async () => {
    return posts;
  },
  ['posts-key'], // keyParts
  { tags: ['posts'] } // tags
);

export async function addPost(title: string) {
  // Simulate delay to make it realistic
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
  posts.push({ id: Date.now().toString(), title });
}
```

### `app/page.tsx`
```typescript
import { getPosts } from './data';
import { createPost } from './actions';

export default async function Home() {
  const posts = await getPosts();

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Posts</h1>
      <ul>
        {posts.map((post) => (
          <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <form action={createPost}>
        <label>
          New Post Title:
          <input type="text" name="title" required style={{ display: 'block', margin: '10px 0' }} />
        </label>
        <button type="submit">Create Post</button>
      </form>
    </main>
  );
}
```
